47 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "92fe000e-8b10-5f6c-a7a8-e9bb8ce2fa57" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290547 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's make the trigonometric functions the subject of each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t=\\frac{x}{2} \\\\ y=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t=\\frac{y}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using double angle formula for cosine and the Pythagorean identity, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t & ={cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =(1-{sin}^{2}⁡t)-{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\operatorname{sin}⁡t=\\frac{x}{2}$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t=\\frac{y}{3}$ into this formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{3} & =1-2{(\\frac{x}{2})}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{y}{3} & =1-2(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}) \\\\ \\frac{y}{3} & =1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2} \\\\ y & =3(1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=3(1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321741 #edb/ref 1080 "b=-1,\\,c=1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321741 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321741 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4b865f1f-3c5c-5985-bbf9-f3e42ab7b33b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322043 #edb/ref 1080 "b=1,\\,c=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322043 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322043 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "71dd4a6f-34e4-573a-9c0e-b15bbfcb0163" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322529 #edb/ref 1080 "b=1,\\,c=1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322529 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322529 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b04c19b3-7728-5118-989a-8a737acbfb86" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322627 #edb/ref 1080 "b=1,\\,c=-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322627 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322627 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "be5e5c90-a85c-57cf-872f