we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(K) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & \\,-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{4+4}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the $3$rd column of the $3\\times 3$ determinant contains two zeros. So, using Laplace expansion along the $3$rd column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(K) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-1)^{1+3}|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4(2-0) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329947 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186329507 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329947 #edb/ref 1069 "q-48993" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329947 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329947 #edb/ref 1071 "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=e.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329947 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4a6705a9-7a56-57af-9eab-fa453a263686" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329947 #edb/ref 1074 "We differentiate using the product rule. Let $u(x)=x$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}.\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=e$ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=e} & =1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\  & =1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡e \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336092 #edb/ref 1080 "III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336092 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336092 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "07b1c5dd-3548-52e8-9ae9-7a7e69e1cbd3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336397 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336397 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336397 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2686c781-1b7c-5eec-90aa-e21536c98faa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336942 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336942 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336942 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "65ffbf8e-c784-56aa-8de3-2eeba3d020ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338061 #edb/ref 1080 "I and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338061 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338061 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e83475f5-b5ac-5c4a-8b55-66347995dbbe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338241 #edb/ref 1080 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338241 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338241 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fb802650-6474-5c4e-a5cd-42a491e290cd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338309 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186336092 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338309 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186336397 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338309 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186336942 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338309 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186338061 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338309 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186338241 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338309 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338309 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338309 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 1759